      "FacilityID": 1000122191,
      "SummaryText": "Executive Summary \u0096 Risk Management Plan\nVertical Cold Storage, LLC \u0096 Canton, MI\nVertical Cold Storage, LLC operates a cold storage facility in Canton, Michigan, utilizing anhydrous ammonia exclusively as a refrigerant in its refrigeration system. This is the only regulated substance on-site.\nOn April 1, 2025, Vertical Cold Storage acquired Arctic Logistics, further expanding our national cold chain network and reinforcing our commitment to food safety and regulatory compliance.\nWe prioritize the safety of our employees, the public, and the environment. Our robust prevention program includes engineering controls, documented procedures, regular employee training, and coordination with local emergency responders, including the Canton Fire Department and Hazmat Team.\nBoth worst-case and alternative-case release scenarios have been modeled using EPA's RMP Comp and are documented on-site.\nWe comply with EPA\u0092s Risk Management Program (40 CFR Part 68), OSHA\u0092s Process Safety Management standard (29 CFR 1910.119), and EPCRA Section 302. Key elements include:\n\u0095\tProcess Safety Information & Hazard Analysis: Maintained and reviewed regularly.\n\u0095\tOperating Procedures & Training: Established procedures with ongoing training and refreshers.\n\u0095\tMechanical Integrity: Scheduled inspections and maintenance by trained personnel.\n\u0095\tManagement of Change: Formalized procedures for any process modifications.\n\u0095\tPre-Startup Reviews & Compliance Audits: Conducted regularly for safety assurance.\n\u0095\tIncident Investigation & Employee Participation: Prompt reviews and open communication.\n\u0095\tContractor Safety: Evaluated and informed of site hazards and emergency procedures.\nVertical Cold Storage has had no reportable ammonia releases in the past five years. We continue to strengthen our safety culture through routine training, emergency drills, and continuous improvement initiatives."
    }
